-- title:
--   Flatness of a standard Proj chart of a graded quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a commutative ring and $A$ a commutative $S$-algebra equipped with an $\mathbb{N}$-grading $\mathcal{A} : \mathbb{N} \to \mathrm{Submodule}\ S\ A$ making it a graded $S$-algebra. Let $I \subseteq A$ be an ideal which is homogeneous in the sense that for every $a \in I$ and every $k$ the $k$-th graded component $(\mathrm{DirectSum.decompose}\ \mathcal{A}\ a\ k : A)$ again lies in $I$, and assume that for every $k$ the $S$-module $\mathcal{A}_k / (I \cap \mathcal{A}_k)$ — formally the quotient of $\mathcal{A}_k$ by the preimage of $I$ (viewed as an $S$-submodule of $A$) under the inclusion $\mathcal{A}_k \hookrightarrow A$ — is flat. Let $d \in \mathbb{N}$ and $f \in \mathcal{A}_d$. Let $J$ be the ideal of the degree-zero homogeneous localisation $\mathrm{Away}\ \mathcal{A}\ f$ generated by all elements of the form $\mathrm{mk}\ y$, where $y$ is a pair of numerator and denominator of the same degree with denominator a power of $f$ and with numerator lying in $I$. Then the composite ring homomorphism $S \to A \to \mathcal{A}_0 \to \mathrm{Away}\ \mathcal{A}\ f \to (\mathrm{Away}\ \mathcal{A}\ f)/J$, given by the structure map of the $S$-algebra $A$, the degree-zero projection, the canonical map from $\mathcal{A}_0$ and the quotient map, is flat, i.e. the target is a flat $S$-module.
--
--   This is the flatness over $\operatorname{Spec} S$ of the standard affine chart $D_+(f)$ of the closed subscheme $\operatorname{Proj}(A/I) \subseteq \operatorname{Proj} A$ cut out by a homogeneous ideal whose graded quotient pieces are flat; the ideal $J$ is the dehomogenisation of $I$ on that chart. It is obtained from the corresponding statement for a graded algebra with flat graded pieces, [`HomogeneousLocalization.Away.flat_fromZeroRingHom_comp_algebraMap_of_forall_flat`](thm.html#HomogeneousLocalization.Away.flat_fromZeroRingHom_comp_algebraMap_of_forall_flat), and is used in the construction of points of the Hilbert functor, via [`AlgebraicGeometry.HilbertFunctor.Point.flat_comp_of_ideal_basicOpen_eq_span`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.HilbertFunctor.Point.flat_comp_of_ideal_basicOpen_eq_span).
